<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 27, 2026</p>

        <h2>1. General Information</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy outlines the handling of data within this private, non-commercial application. The software operates exclusively for internal testing, personal automation, and development validation.</p>

        <h2>2. Data Collection and Processing</h2>
        <p>This application does not collect, track, aggregate, sell, or process personal information from end users, visitors, or third parties.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>API Access Tokens:</strong> Authentication tokens (e.g., OAuth access tokens) obtained from platform providers are stored securely and encrypted in a local environment solely for executing authorized API requests.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Handling:</strong> Any data fetched via platform APIs (such as account metrics or video publishing statuses) is processed temporarily and in memory to execute personal commands.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Data Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
        <p>No data retrieved or generated by this application is ever shared with, sold to, or distributed to third-party advertisers, data brokers, or external analytics services.</p>

        <h2>4. Data Storage, Security, and Retention</h2>
        <p>All processing occurs within administrator-controlled infrastructure. Authentication tokens are retained only as long as required for active API connectivity. Removing application credentials or revoking OAuth permissions via the platform dashboard immediately terminates access and deletes cached tokens.</p>

        <h2>5. Third-Party API Policies</h2>
        <p>This application interacts with third-party APIs. For details on how those platforms manage user privacy, please refer to their respective official policies (such as the TikTok Privacy Policy).</p>

        <h2>6. Contact</h2>
        <p>For any privacy inquiries related to this development project, please reach out directly to the application administrator.</p>

        <div class="footer">
            <p>&copy; 2026 Private Developer Project. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
